 the Next.js (App Router) production service under\n`services/frontend/` ONLY. Do NOT touch anything under `tests/`,\n`docs/`, or `true-bdd/`. Do NOT modify the test.\n\nCreate each file below with the **Write** tool (all are new files).\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### Change #1: Node/package manifest\n**File:** `services/frontend/package.json`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev -p 3000\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"next\": \"14.2.23\",\n    \"react\": \"^18.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^18.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.4.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^20\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^18\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^18\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Change #2: TypeScript config (referenced by the architecture quality gate)\n**File:** `services/frontend/tsconfig.json`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [{ \"name\": \"next\" }],\n    \"paths\": { \"@/*\": [\"./*\"] }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Change #3: Minimal Next.js config\n**File:** `services/frontend/next.config.mjs`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```js\n/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {};\n\nexport default nextConfig;\n```\n\n### Change #4: Root layout (App Router requires an html/body root)\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/layout.tsx`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'Frontend',\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Change #5: Home page — the single `h1` the test asserts\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/page.tsx`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nexport default function Home() {\n  return <h1>Hello world</h1>;\n}\n```\nNOTE: This page must render exactly ONE `<h1>` and its full text content\nmust be `Hello world` (Playwright's `toHaveText('Hello world')` normalizes\nwhitespace but matches the whole element and fails if more than one `h1`\nexists). Do not add extra `h1` elements or surrounding text.\n\n### Change #6: Dockerfile that builds and serves on port 3000\n**File:** `services/frontend/Dockerfile`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nCOPY package.json ./\nRUN npm install\n\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\n\nEXPOSE 3000\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\nNOTE: `docker-compose.yaml` sets `build.context: ./services/frontend`, so\nthe Dockerfile must live at `services/frontend/Dockerfile` (its default\nlocation). `next start -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0` binds all interfaces so the\n`3000:3000` port mapping reaches it and the Playwright `webServer` URL\n`http://127.0.0.1:3000` responds.\n\n### Change #7: Docker ignore (keep host artifacts out of the image build)\n**File:** `services/frontend/.dockerignore`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```\nnode_modules\n.next\nnpm-debug.log\n```\n\n## Why this passes\n1. `docker compose up --build frontend` now finds `services/frontend/Dockerfile`,\n   installs deps, runs `next build`, and starts `next start` on `0.0.0.0:3000`.